# The Goodix touchscreen on the MidiReef kiosk panel delivers raw touch
# coordinates rotated 90° clockwise relative to the DSI output's own
# "normal" (0°) framebuffer orientation — confirmed empirically by attaching
# Chromium's remote debugger and comparing physical corner taps against the
# clientX/clientY it actually received (see git history for the calibration
# session). Without this, the compositor's own per-output rotation
# (Settings → Display, server/src/display.rs → deploy/bin/midireef-display)
# only ever lines touch up with ONE specific rotation by accident; any other
# choice shows touch off by 90/180/270° from what's on screen.
#
# This calibration matrix (a 270°/-90° rotation) corrects raw touch
# coordinates back into the output's normal orientation, so labwc's own
# automatic touch-to-output transform (see `<touch mapToOutput="">` in
# rc.xml, deliberately left empty to auto-bind to whichever output actually
# exists — output names like "DSI-1"/"DSI-2" have been observed to change
# across boots) then applies any of 0/90/180/270 correctly on top.
#
# Matched by capability rather than device name/path, since both have been
# observed to change; safe because this kiosk only ever has one touchscreen.
#
# NOTE: labwc/libinput only reads this when the touch device is (re)opened —
# it does NOT pick up a live change for a device it already has open.
# Reboot (or otherwise restart the compositor) after ever changing this.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_TOUCHSCREEN}=="1", ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="0 1 0 -1 0 1"
